    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nGrep and grep live functionality will also search the .git/ folder, which isn't really useful. It also pollutes search results.\r\n\r\nAn effective solution could be passing `--glob=.git/*` to ripgrep, but there are other ways to prevent searching .git folders.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nnightly\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. :Pick grep some string that's in the .git folder\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\ndon't search .git folder\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nsearches .git folder",
